# Argon OS — Security Edition
# Everything from the XFCE edition (this variant's parent), plus the
# standard Kali tool selection. The tools come unmodified from the Kali
# repositories Argon already builds against — this edition simply
# preinstalls what the standard edition leaves one `apt install` away.
#
# kali-linux-default is Kali's own "default tool selection" metapackage:
# the set a stock Kali installation ships with (nmap, wireshark,
# metasploit, burpsuite, sqlmap, john, hydra, aircrack-ng, ...). Using the
# metapackage rather than a hand-picked list means the selection tracks
# Kali's, and updates with it.
#
# NOTE the size: this roughly doubles the ISO. GitHub release assets cap
# at 2 GiB per file, so CI publishes Security Edition images split into
# parts (see .github/workflows/build-iso.yml) — download all parts and
# concatenate, per the release notes.
kali-linux-default

## Argon defaults still apply. In particular:
##  * UFW stays deny-incoming and no service listens by default — the
##    tools are installed, not started.
##  * AppArmor, DNS-over-TLS, MAC randomization etc. are unchanged.
